            <ArticleTitle>[Pneumooxyhemographic method for the comprehensive study of circulation and respiration].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>62-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over 3000 pneumoxyhaemogrammes were recorded in 1840 persons. Periods, types and criteria of pathology were differentiated in the structure of the pneumoxyhaemogramme. The method permits to reveal early forms of cardiovascular pathology. It is applicable for the examination of both normals and patients for early diagnosis of cardiovascular pathology, for the control of the therapeutic effect, and for a dynamic observation in the course of a dispensary screening.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
